## Objective
- Implement phase-096: add first-class Redblue date/time values (`Value::Date`) and durations (`Value::Duration`) with comparison, subtraction, calendar arithmetic, properties, and SPEC.md timezone/overflow documentation.
- Finish the phase in continuation mode: run the four gates, write `phases/phase-096/REPORT.md`, then say DONE.

## Important Details
- Working dir: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`. Only read/write inside it; scratch under `./target/tmp/`.
- Do not touch `.github/workflows/`, `rbops/`, `.opencode/agent/`, `rbops/phases.json`. `must_touch: [src/]`.
- Do not weaken/delete/ignore tests; no new `allow(clippy::` suppressions.
- Full suite is `cargo test --all-targets` (67 binaries, ~15 min). Targeted tests during iteration only.
- Gate commands: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --all-targets`; `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-096"` (no `rbops/` inside checkout).
- Finding reproduced with: `printf 'say time.date(2024, 1, 1)\n' > target/tmp/repro_date.rb && cargo run --quiet --bin rb -- run target/tmp/repro_date.rb` → `RuntimeError: Module 'time' has no function 'date'`.
- Starting tree was clean; remote `origin/rbops-wip/phase-096` checkpoint commit `9f589d3` had no file changes, so no prior partial work was usable.
- Design decisions: timezone-naive `NaiveDateTime`; month/year arithmetic clamps to last day of target month (`Jan 31 +1mo → Feb 29/28`, `Feb 29 +1yr → Feb 28`); fixed days/hours/minutes/seconds (no DST); date/duration vs number ordering is a catchable Runtime error; equality across kinds is `no` (consistent with existing language).
- Registered new builtins: `time_date`, `time_datetime`, `time_duration`, `time_add_years`, `time_add_months`, `time_add_days`, `time_add_hours`, `time_add_minutes`, `time_add_seconds`.
- Date properties: `year`, `month`, `day`, `hour`, `minute`, `second`, `weekday`. Duration properties: `days`, `hours`, `minutes`, `seconds`, `total_seconds`, `nanoseconds`. Unknown property → `nothing`.
- Display: date `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`; duration e.g. `1 day, 1 hour`, zero `0 seconds`, negative leading `-`.
- JSON: date → quoted display text; duration → total seconds number.
- Known pending code-quality issue: `compare()` in `src/runtime.rs` still uses `unreachable!` in the final `match op` arm; replace with a returned Runtime error to avoid a panic-path review finding.
- Minor known inconsistency: duration `.nanoseconds` is always non-negative even for negative spans; consider signing it.
- SPEC example originally used `span.days`/`span.total_seconds`, which broke `stdlib_module_names_test` because it scans fenced code blocks for `module.member`; fixed by using `to_text(...)` and only `time.*` dotted calls in code blocks.

